    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nA wonderful opportunity to acquire a substantial detached family residence enjoying an enviable position on a mature and exceptionally private site along Leopardstown Road. Set behind mature hedging and approached via a generous, gravelled driveway providing ample off-street parking, Woodleigh offers bright, well-proportioned accommodation ideally suited to modern family living. The property has been lovingly maintained over the years and presents an exciting opportunity for purchasers to further modernise and personalise to their own requirements.\n\nExtending to approximately 255 sq. m/ 2745 sq. ft the accommodation is both spacious and versatile. An inviting entrance hall gives access to a magnificent sitting room overlooking the rear garden, a comfortable family room to the front, a study ideal for home working and a formal dining room. To the rear lies a large kitchen/breakfast room with Aga and direct access to the patio and garden. A utility room, storeroom and guest w.c. complete the ground floor accommodation. \n\nUpstairs, there are four generous bedrooms together with a family bathroom. The principal suite is a particular feature, comprising an exceptionally spacious bedroom with extensive wardrobe space, a separate dressing room and ensuite bathroom. Originally laid out as two bedrooms, this area could easily be reinstated to provide a fifth bedroom should additional accommodation be required.\n\nA particular feature of Woodleigh is its magnificent north-westerly facing rear garden. Wonderfully private and bordered by mature trees, specimen planting and established hedging, it provides a peaceful setting rarely found so close to an array of amenities. A large patio terrace enjoys sunshine throughout the afternoon and into the evening, creating the perfect setting for outdoor dining and entertaining.\n\nOffering space, privacy and an excellent family-friendly layout in a highly convenient location, Woodleigh is sure to appeal to discerning purchasers seeking a forever home in one of South Dublin's most established residential settings.\n\nLeopardstown Road is a highly regarded residential road of mature, quality family homes in the heart of Foxrock. The property is within walking distance of nearby Foxrock Village with its specialist shops and the popular Gables restaurant. There are numerous recreational amenities in the area to include nearby Foxrock golf club and Leopardstown racecourse. There is an excellent selection of shopping facilities nearby to include Carrickmines Retail Park, Cornelscourt shopping centre and Dundrum Town Centre is easily accessible. There are a range of highly sought after secondary schools within easy reach of Leopardstown Road. This is a first class residential location where houses of this calibre offering such potential rarely come to the market. The N11 QBC together with the Luas at Sandyford provide easy access to Dublin city centre. It is also easily accessible to nearby Sandyford Business Park and the M50 interchange providing access to all points north, south, east and west."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hallway - 2.4m x 6.27m\nWith tiled floor, recessed lighting\n\nDining Room - 3.56m x 5.79m\noverlooking front, fitted carpet, chandelier light fitting, centre rose, ceiling coving\n\nGuest WC - \nwith tiled floor, WC, wash hand basin with fitted press beneath.\n\nDrawing Room - 5.07m x 6.02m\nwith picture window overlooking rear garden, fitted carpet, recessed lighting, open fireplace with marble hearth and surround, door to rear garden\n\nSitting Room - 5.12m x 5.38m\nwith open marble fireplace, fitted carpet, two picture windows overlooking the front garden, attractive mantelpiece with decorative tiled surround, gas fire inset.\n\nKitchen/ Breakfast room - 3.56m x 7.65m\nwith tiled floor, good range of floor and eye level kitchen units, with tiled splashback and centre island, Belling dishwasher, single drainer sink with chrome fittings, oil Aga, Beko fridge, Synergie multi function double oven, recessed lighting, exposed beams, Moffat integrated four-ring hob, French doors to rear garden\n\nUtility - 2.36m x 5.06m\nwith tiled floor, Bosch washing machine, door to hot press, door to boiler house with gas boiler, press containing, fitted shelving, storeroom.\n\nStoreroom - 2.36m x 3.97m\nto the front, with painted concrete floor, door to front garden with front yard area which contains the oil tank and bins.\n\nOffice - 2.46m x 4.36m\nwith a range of built in shelving units, fitted mahogany desk, picture window overlooking rear garden, ceiling coving\n\nUpstairs - \n\n\nMaster Bedroom/Bedroom 1 - 3.56m x 7.13m\noriginally two bedrooms, with fitted carpet, extensive range of built in wardrobes, recessed lighting, dressing area with wood floor.\n\nEnsuite Bathroom - \nFully tiled, bath with shower attachment over, WC, range of his and hers matching wash hand basins with fitted mirror over and storage cupboards beneath.\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.51m x 5.30m\ngood sized double with wooden floor, window to front, wall mounted mirror, wall mounted shelf, modern three pointed spot lighting.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.51m x 4.22m\ngood sized double with fitted carpet, window to the front and modern three point light fitting.\n\nFamily Bathroom - 2.06m x 2.51m\nWith tiled floor, step in shower with Mira shower head, shower fittings, WC, pedestal wash hand basin , chrome fittings, wall mounted dual matching lights overhead.\n\nBedroom 4 - 2.4m x 2.75m\nSingle bedroom to the front with fitted carpet and built in wardrobe.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Detached family residence extending to approximately 255 sq.m/ 2745 sq.ft</li><li>Rear garden enjoys complete privacy and seclusion yet offering further potential to develop subject to planning permission</li><li>Fitted carpets, curtains and kitchen appliances included in the sale.</li><li>Three reception rooms </li><li>Separate study/home office </li><li>Four-bedroom layout with potential to reinstate a fifth bedroom </li><li>Principal suite with dressing room and ensuite </li><li>Oil-fired central heating </li><li>Double-glazed windows throughout </li><li>Off-street parking for four cars </li><li>Central Park Luas stop 5 minutes' walk </li><li>Highly sought-after Leopardstown Road location.</li><li>Aircoach nearby </li><li>Bus directly outside to Blackrock, Dun Laoghaire and beyond.</ul>"
